P19-CONV-001 pre-implementation measurement, seed 202611072
==============================================================================

Q1  per-face decomposition  max(phi,0) + min(phi,0) == phi
    random finite phi      : 200000 trials, 0 mismatches
    edge values            : 8 checked, 0 mismatches  
    wall face (phi = 0.0)  : max=0.0 min=0.0  -> contributes 0.0
    NOTE  -0.0 arises only if a producer COMPUTES a wall flux instead
          of setting the table's zero; max(-0.0,0.0)=-0.0 min=-0.0

Q2  rowSum(A) vs face-order divergence of phi  (the cross-check oracle)
    20000 meshes: bit-exact on 2369 (11.85%)
    worst relative gap: 4.34385e+13   (denominator = sum |row entry|)
    at mesh shape: (7, 8)
    => the row-sum oracle is a TOLERANCE check, not a bit-exact one.

Q3  reverse flow:  A(-phi) == A(phi)^T   for divergence-free phi
    3a 1D chain, uniform flux, INTERIOR rows:
       2000 chains, transpose exact on 2000 (100.00%)
    3b general mesh, A(-phi) == A(phi)^T - diag(div phi):
       5000 meshes, exact on 714 (14.28%), worst relative 1.17314e-07

Q4  boundedness: dominance deficit vs the cell divergence
    8000 meshes: deficit == -divergence within 1e-14 on 8000 (100.00%)
    worst relative departure: 0
    => boundedness is CONDITIONAL on a conservative phi, and the
       deficit is the divergence, so no second number is needed.

